@startuml CI/CD Pipeline

title Deployment View - CI/CD (GitHub Actions -> GHCR)

actor "Developer" as dev
participant "GitHub\n(main branch / tag)" as github
participant "GitHub Actions" as ci
participant "GitHub Container\nRegistry (GHCR)" as ghcr
participant "Staging host\n(Docker Compose)" as staging

== Quality Gate (every push to main / PR) ==

dev -> github: Push commit or open PR
github -> ci: Trigger workflows
ci -> ci: Backend (dotnet.yml): build, then\nUnit + Architecture + Integration + Visual tests\n(Integration/Visual boot the Aspire stack)
ci -> ci: Frontend (frontend.yml): lint + build
ci -> ci: Lint (lint.yml): ASCII dashes + EditorConfig

== Docs (push to main, docs/** only) ==

dev -> github: Push to main (docs/**)
github -> ci: Trigger docs.yml
ci -> ci: asciidoctor build (arc42 -> HTML5)
ci -> github: Deploy docs to GitHub Pages

== Release (version tag push) ==

dev -> github: Push tag vX.Y.Z (or vX.Y.Z-rc.N)
github -> ci: Trigger publish.yml
ci -> ci: Run full test suite
ci -> ghcr: Build + push backend, frontend, keycloak images\nghcr.io/maik-hasler/einsatzbereit-<component>
ci -> staging: Deploy RC to staging (SSH: docker compose pull + up)\nhealth-gated, auto-rollback on failure

note over ci,ghcr
	One tag (vX.Y.Z) releases all three components at the same version.
	RC tags (-rc.N) publish images and deploy to staging without moving 'latest'.
	See VERSIONING.md for the full strategy.
end note

@enduml
